<a name="sec1"></a>
<h2>1. Executive Summary & Purpose</h2>
<p>
  <strong>Check Sky Light</strong> is an open, empirical civilian sky diagnostics and aerospace deconfliction platform. It bridges the divide between naive skepticism and uncritical credulity by providing citizen scientists, field researchers, and observers with a calibrated, real-time sensor instrument in their pocket.
</p>
<p>
  Traditional sky observation apps either function as passive crowdsourced reporting forms or closed proprietary black boxes. Check Sky Light transforms a standard modern smartphone into an active aerospace diagnostic station by fusing:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Device Sensor Fusion:</strong> Hardware-calibrated IMU orientation (pitch, azimuth, roll, angular velocity), high-frame-rate optical capture, and acoustic microphone preservation.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-Domain Airspace Telemetry:</strong> Real-time cross-referencing against live ADS-B civilian/military transponders, NOAA weather balloon soundings, and NORAD Low Earth Orbit (LEO) satellite trajectories.</li>
  <li><strong>The Parallax Panel (Tri-Model AI Architecture):</strong> Collaborative cross-examination between three independent frontier AI engines (<strong>Gemini</strong>, <strong>Claude</strong>, and <strong>Luna</strong>) enforcing strict empirical falsifiability.</li>
  <li><strong>The Dual-Lens Analytical Framework:</strong> Simultaneous evaluation under <strong>Lens A (Classical Fluid Dynamics & Aerospace Baseline)</strong> and <strong>Lens B (Theoretical Spacetime Metric Manipulation)</strong>.</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec2"></a>
<h2>2. The Four Operational Pillars</h2>
<p>
  Check Sky Light is architected around four distinct operational modules:
</p>

<a name="sec2-1"></a>
<h3>Pillar 1: TARGET (Optical AR Tracking HUD)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Real-Time Reticle HUD:</strong> Overlays high-contrast azimuth (0°–360°), elevation pitch (-90° to +90°), roll, and angular tracking rates (°/sec) directly onto the live camera stream.</li>
  <li><strong>Telephoto & Optical Filtration:</strong> Digital/optical crop-zoom controls (1x, 2x, 3x, 5x) combined with Day-HDR, Night-Starlight, and High-Contrast optical filters.</li>
  <li><strong>Acoustic Silence Tenet:</strong> Operates completely silent by default (synthesizers and shutter sounds muted) so the microphone records clean, uncontaminated ambient acoustic signatures (Doppler shifts, infrasound, propulsion hums, or absolute silence).</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec2-2"></a>
<h3>Pillar 2: RADAR (Live Airspace Deconfliction)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>ADS-B Transponder Integration:</strong> Live tracking of commercial airliners, private aviation, and unblocked transponders within the observer's visual radius.</li>
  <li><strong>NOAA Weather Balloon Tracking:</strong> Live telemetry from national weather service radiosonde launches (frequency, ascent rate, altitude MSL).</li>
  <li><strong>LEO Satellite Ephemeris:</strong> Orbital trajectory vectors for Starlink trains, the International Space Station (ISS), and prominent orbital debris.</li>
  <li><strong>Deconfliction-First Principle:</strong> Automatically weeds out known conventional flights before any anomaly claim is considered.</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec2-3"></a>
<h3>Pillar 3: ANALYZE (Multi-Lens Forensic AI Lab)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Digital Media & CGI Forensics:</strong> Screens uploaded images and video frames for synthetic diffusion noise, edge matting splines, 3D camera tracking drift, and post-production keyframing.</li>
  <li><strong>Dual-Lens Analytical Engine:</strong> Tests footage against both <strong>Lens A</strong> (FAA anti-collision strobes, aerodynamic surfaces, Newtonian drag) and <strong>Lens B</strong> (Metric manipulation, vacuum shearing, absence of sonic booms).</li>
  <li><strong>Tri-Model Consensus:</strong> Multi-agent validation across Gemini, Claude, and Luna to eliminate single-model hallucinations.</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec2-4"></a>
<h3>Pillar 4: REPORT (Diagnostic Dossiers & Archival)</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Automotive Diagnostic Trouble Codes (DTC):</strong> Assigns standardized fault codes (e.g., <code>DTC P0312</code>, <code>DTC P0420</code>) to communicate encounter severity and category instantly.</li>
  <li><strong>Multi-Observer Triangulation:</strong> Calculates true 3D geometric altitude (ft MSL) and slant range (mi) using simultaneous two-point witness sightline intersections.</li>
  <li><strong>Audit-Ready Export:</strong> Generates tamper-evident, publication-grade PDF dossiers complete with sensor provenance stamps ready for submission to academic and governmental repositories (AARO, SUAPS, SCU).</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec3"></a>
<h2>3. The Power of Collaborative AI: The Parallax Panel</h2>
<p>
  A cornerstone strength of Check Sky Light is its rejection of single-model "black box" AI. Instead, it utilizes the <strong>Parallax Panel</strong>—a collaborative tri-model review methodology:
</p>

<table style="width:100%; border:1pt solid #cbd5e1;">
  <tr>
    <th style="width:33%;">GEMINI (Vision & Sensor)</th>
    <th style="width:33%;">CLAUDE (Epistemology & Logic)</th>
    <th style="width:33%;">LUNA (Telemetry & Deconfliction)</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>Real-time mobile IMU parsing, optical tracking & live multi-modal vision extraction.</td>
    <td>Methodological rigor, peer-review audit, logic validation & citation verification.</td>
    <td>Adversarial stress-testing, synthetic media elimination & conventional boundary enforcement.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<a name="sec3-1"></a>
<h3>The "Secret" Diagnostic Code: DTC P0312</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>3:</strong> Three independent neural architectures (Gemini, Claude, Luna)</li>
  <li><strong>1:</strong> One unified empirical consensus</li>
  <li><strong>2:</strong> Two simultaneous analytical lenses (Classical Aerospace vs. Metric Manipulation)</li>
  <li><strong>Status Readout:</strong> <code>DTC P0312: DUAL-LENS PARALLAX RESOLVED</code>. When an encounter receives DTC P0312, it signifies that all conventional mundane candidates have been systematically eliminated and the data meets the threshold of a genuine anomaly.</li>
</ul>

