<a name="sec4-2"></a>
<h3>Detailed Application Critiques</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Check Sky Light (v3.6) — 9.5/10:</strong> Total convergence. Fuses live AR tracking, immediate multi-source airspace deconfliction, multi-model AI forensic evaluation, and formal PDF dossiers into an accessible, zero-install mobile application. (Limitation: Handheld tool; does not provide 24/7 all-sky stationary camera surveillance).</li>
  <li><strong>Enigma Labs — 5.5/10:</strong> High social polish and strong funding, but functions as a closed "black box". Scoring relies on opaque proprietary algorithms without peer review. Lacks a live optical AR telemetry HUD, multi-model AI consensus, and downloadable raw mathematical triangulation dossiers.</li>
  <li><strong>Sky360 Network — 6.6/10:</strong> Exceptional open-source citizen science community with continuous 24/7 all-sky coverage. However, the high financial and technical barrier to entry (specialized rooftop camera rigs) makes it inaccessible for everyday mobile field use.</li>
  <li><strong>UFODAP — 5.5/10:</strong> Outstanding multi-spectral scientific hardware (optical, RF, magnetic), but dated software interface, zero mobile utility, and costs thousands of dollars.</li>
  <li><strong>Skywatcher.ai — 6.8/10:</strong> Leading autonomous CV tracking algorithms, but tailored for enterprise/research installations rather than spontaneous civilian field encounters.</li>
  <li><strong>MUFON CMS Mobile — 2.7/10:</strong> Form-based questionnaire backlog. No live camera sensor integration, no live ADS-B deconfliction, and investigations take months to process manually.</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec5"></a>
<h2>5. The Evolving 5-Tier Empirical Knowledge Base</h2>
<p>
  To maintain scientific rigor and prevent contamination from internet folklore, Check Sky Light anchors its diagnostics against five authoritative scientific tiers:
</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Tier I: Official Government & Defense Declassification:</strong> AARO (aaro.mil), NASA UAP Independent Study, CNES/GEIPAN (France), ODNI threat assessments.</li>
  <li><strong>Tier II: Academic & Institutional Scientific Bodies:</strong> Society for UAP Studies (SUAPS) / Limina Journal, Scientific Coalition for UAP Studies (SCU), The Galileo Project (Harvard), AIAA UAPIOC.</li>
  <li><strong>Tier III: Autonomous Sky Observation Networks:</strong> Skywatcher.ai, Sky360 Network, UFODAP, Project Hessdalen (Norway, recording since 1983).</li>
  <li><strong>Tier IV: Spaceflight, Telemetry & Ephemeris Deconfliction:</strong> Space-Track / Celestrak (NORAD 18th Space Defense Squadron), ADS-B Exchange, NOAA NEXRAD dual-pol radar.</li>
  <li><strong>Tier V: Theoretical Metric & Decoupled Physics:</strong> Alcubierre (1994) warp metric, Lentz (2021) positive-energy solitons, Bobrick & Martire (2021), boundary-layer vacuum shearing models.</li>
</ul>

<a name="sec6"></a>
<h2>6. Cockpit Archetypes & DTC Diagnostic System</h2>
<p>
  Tapping the top-left <strong>Check Engine icon</strong> allows observers to switch between four customizable cockpit instrument displays:
</p>
<ol>
  <li><strong>Black Project Flight Deck (Default):</strong> Obsidian Base (<code>#08090C</code>) with Master Caution Amber (<code>#FF9500</code>) and Mil-Spec Green (<code>#30D158</code>). Inspired by Special Access Program (SAP) aerospace testbeds and fighter annunciator tiles.</li>
  <li><strong>Retro OBD-II Diagnostic Dash:</strong> CRT Gunmetal (<code>#0B0E14</code>) with Vacuum Fluorescent Display (VFD) Neon Cyan (<code>#00F2FE</code>) and Halogen Orange (<code>#FF5722</code>). 1984 concept car digital cluster with diagnostic trouble screens.</li>
  <li><strong>Gen-3 NVG & FLIR Thermal:</strong> Night Forest Base (<code>#030B05</code>) with 530nm Monochromatic Phosphor Green (<code>#39FF14</code>). Replicates looking through PVS-14 night vision goggles or an electro-optical turret with milliradian tick scales.</li>
  <li><strong>Observatory Starlight Mode:</strong> True OLED Black (<code>#000000</code>) with Deep Celestial Ruby Red (<code>#FF3B30</code>). Pure astronomy red lighting that completely preserves human rhodopsin (dark-adapted night vision) during outdoor fieldwork.</li>
</ol>

<a name="sec7"></a>
<h2>7. Summary: Why Check Sky Light Sets a New Benchmark</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Scientific Integrity Over Sensationalism:</strong> False positives and conventional deconflictions are celebrated as successes, not disappointments.</li>
  <li><strong>No Proprietary Black Boxes:</strong> Every sensor calculation, trigonometric triangulation vector, and AI consensus check is transparent, inspectable, and exportable.</li>
  <li><strong>Zero Barrier to Entry:</strong> Operates instantly on modern smartphone browsers without requiring expensive proprietary hardware rigs.</li>
  <li><strong>Collaborative AI Governance:</strong> Continually cross-examined by the tri-model peer review of Gemini, Claude, and Luna to ensure technology remains an uncompromising servant of truth.</li>
</ul>

<div class="footer">
  <p><strong>Check Sky Light v3.6.0</strong> • Open Civilian Aerospace Diagnostics & Deconfliction</p>
